    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d278">

                <pb facs="0410" n="340" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg340"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Dayton.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 158.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State.</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-05-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 12, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> It will be proper for you to inform Mr.
                    Thouvenel that I have communicated the substance of his explanations given to
                    you on the subject of Mexican complications to Mr. Romero, excluding, however,
                    all that part of the explanations which was stated to you by Mr. Thouvenel to be
                    confidential. A copy of my communication to Mr. Romero is annexed.</p>
                <p>The frankness and distinctness which we have maintained throughout with all
                    parties on this grave subject have seemed to require this proceeding.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William L. Dayton</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
